<title>JAPAN: Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</title>
<headline>Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mikuni and Co Ltd said on Friday it had assigned the following preliminary ratings to planned bond issues:</p>
<p>-AA-</p>
<p>Fujitsu Ltd, 50 billion yen unsecured due 2003.</p>
<p>50 billion yen unsecured due 2006.</p>
<p>-A-</p>
<p>Seino Transportation Co Ltd, 20 billion Euro yen unsecured convertible due 2004.  </p>
<p>-BBB-</p>
<p>Melco Inc, 0.225 billion yen unsecured with warrants due 2001.</p>
<p>Miura Co Ltd, $100 million unsecured with warrants due 2000.</p>
<p>-BB-</p>
<p>Heiwado Co Ltd, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2001.</p>
<p>Itochu Fuel Corp, 5 billion yen unsecured due 2000.</p>
<p>5 billion yen unsecured due 2002.</p>
<p>Oji Paper Co Ltd, 40 billion yen unsecured due 2003.  </p>
<p>-BB-</p>
<p>Konica Corp, 5 billion yen unsecured due 2001.</p>
<p>5 billion yen unsecured due 2002.</p>
<p>West Japan Railway Co, 25 billion yen mortgaged due 2006. 30 billion yen mortgaged due 2016.</p>
<p>-B-</p>
<p>Tokyu Land Corp, 20 billion yen unsecured due 2003.</p>
<p>-CCC-</p>
<p>Koken Boring Machine Co Ltd, 3 billion yen</p>
<p>unsecured convertible due 2000, private placement.</p>
</text>
